content.text:
All 17 errors are addressed at their root cause, in two edits:

**1. `server/_core/logger.ts:226` — the TS2345 at line 16.**
`LogDomain` is an explicit allowlist union of domain names. `'alert-analytics'` was simply missing from it, so I added it next to its sibling `'alert-sse'`. Widening the union can't affect any other file.

**2. `server/emotional-geometry-runtime/alert-analytics.ts` — the 16 TS18047s.**
`getDb()` returns `PostgresJsDatabase | null` (server/db.ts:144-154 — it returns `null` when `DATABASE_URL` is unset), and all 16 errors were `db.select/update/insert` calls on that possibly-null handle across 7 functions.

Rather than 7 copies of a null check — several of which would have to duplicate large fallback literals like the 11-field empty `AlertSummaryStats` — I added a `requireDb()` helper that narrows once:

```ts
type AnalyticsDb = NonNullable<Awaited<ReturnType<typeof getDb>>>;

async function requireDb(): Promise<AnalyticsDb> {
  const db = await getDb();
  if (!db) {
    throw new DatabaseUnavailableError('Database unavailable: alert analytics requires a database connection');
  }
  return db;
}
```

and switched all 7 `const db = await getDb()` sites to `await requireDb()`. Every one of those sites already sits inside a `try/catch` that logs and returns a safe empty result, so a missing database now routes into that same existing degraded path instead of dereferencing null. `DatabaseUnavailableError` is the error type `server/db.ts` already throws for this condition, and the `NonNullable<Awaited<...>>` narrowing mirrors the existing `Exclude<Awaited<ReturnType<typeof getDb>>, null>` idiom at server/db.ts:171. No `any`, no suppression comments, no deleted code.

**Verification — not completed, and I want to be explicit about that.** I could not run `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json`. The first attempt was refused by the `routing-gate.sh` hook; I cleared that by writing the routing request the hook itself prescribed, but the retry then returned "This command requires approval" with no approver present. The serena language-server diagnostics tool was likewise never permission-granted. Read-only `grep` did run, and confirms all 7 call sites are converted and no bare `getDb()` dereference remains.

So the reasoning is verified but the compiler is not. What I can state with confidence: the error count matches exactly (16 `db.*` dereferences + 1 domain literal = 17), and no exported signature changed — the helper is module-local and the union only widened — so no new error can appear in another file. What I can't state: that tsc actually reports zero. If you can approve the typecheck command or the diagnostics tool, I'll run it and confirm.

One thing I left alone deliberately: `const conditions: any[]` at `getIncidents` (line ~439) is pre-existing `any` that was not among the 17 errors. Tightening it to `SQL[]` is a reasonable follow-up but is outside this task's scope and would risk introducing new errors I can't currently check.
